WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.600
This video shows how to read the Results
view of a run.

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:09.027
The run of this video is the run of Run
streamflow:

00:00:09.027 --> 00:00:15.210
the basin 02070002, 2000 to 2015, with a
warm-up of three years.

00:00:15.711 --> 00:00:17.511
Click Results in the left column.

00:00:17.711 --> 00:00:19.221
The view has three columns.

00:00:20.155 --> 00:00:22.150
The left column sums the run up:

00:00:22.150 --> 00:00:26.015
Output checks, Water balance, average year
and Output folders.

00:00:26.518 --> 00:00:29.827
The middle column shows the basin as a
block on its relief,

00:00:29.827 --> 00:00:31.398
and the daily flow under it.

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:36.014
The right column gives the counts of the
basin or of one subbasin,

00:00:36.014 --> 00:00:39.630
the values of the day shown, and a table
of the subbasins.

00:00:40.131 --> 00:00:44.291
The box Basin at the top of the left
column chooses what the view shows.

00:00:44.491 --> 00:00:46.561
It lists the basins that have results.

00:00:47.062 --> 00:00:50.872
Output checks is a short table of checks
on the output of the run.

00:00:51.373 --> 00:00:55.385
Water balance, average year gives parts of
the water balance of

00:00:55.385 --> 00:00:58.633
the land in mm and as a share of the
precipitation.

00:00:59.133 --> 00:01:02.813
The middle column draws the basin as a
block on its relief,

00:01:02.813 --> 00:01:06.493
with its streams as blue lines and its
outlet as a red dot.

00:01:06.693 --> 00:01:10.113
The color of each subbasin is its value on
the day shown,

00:01:10.113 --> 00:01:12.753
and the date of that day stands beside
Play.

00:01:13.254 --> 00:01:16.404
Two bands on the sides of the block show
soil water,

00:01:16.404 --> 00:01:18.343
the upper band, and groundwater,

00:01:18.343 --> 00:01:22.584
the lower band, in millimetres, for each
subbasin on the basin's edge.

00:01:22.784 --> 00:01:27.314
Here soil water is the value of the month,
and groundwater the value of the year.

00:01:27.514 --> 00:01:30.564
A band is darker and taller where the
value is higher.

00:01:31.064 --> 00:01:33.534
Choose a value in the list Color by:

00:01:33.534 --> 00:01:36.964
flow, runoff, ET, soil water, snow or
groundwater.

00:01:38.595 --> 00:01:39.435
Click Play.

00:01:39.635 --> 00:01:43.075
The date moves through the run, and the
subbasins change color.

00:01:45.326 --> 00:01:46.646
Click Pause to stop.

00:01:47.903 --> 00:01:52.673
The right column gives the same six values
for the day shown, under On and the date.

00:01:53.173 --> 00:01:57.223
Click a subbasin on the block, or a row of
the table of subbasins.

00:01:58.336 --> 00:02:01.557
The chart now draws the flow from that
subbasin,

00:02:01.557 --> 00:02:04.710
and the right column gives the subbasin's
area,

00:02:04.710 --> 00:02:07.528
the area that drains to it, its elevation,

00:02:07.528 --> 00:02:10.816
and its numbers of HRUs, channels and
reservoirs.

00:02:11.318 --> 00:02:13.208
Click Entire basin to go back.

00:02:14.909 --> 00:02:18.869
To look at a part of the period, click
Zoom and draw a box on the chart.

00:02:25.142 --> 00:02:27.222
Zoom out shows the whole period again.

00:02:28.908 --> 00:02:32.672
The table under the chart gives the mean
flow, the highest flow,

00:02:32.672 --> 00:02:35.612
the low flow and the high flow of the
point shown,

00:02:35.612 --> 00:02:39.198
and the mean flow as a depth over the land
that drains to it.

00:02:39.698 --> 00:02:44.384
The table of subbasins in the right column
lists every subbasin with its area,

00:02:44.384 --> 00:02:47.868
the area that drains to it, and its flow
on the day shown.

00:02:48.370 --> 00:02:51.700
The values of each month and each year are
not on the page.

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:54.650
The rest of the chapter reads them from
the files.
